cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SPECTRA, please cite this software/data record; a paper citation will be added here once the accompanying paper is published."
type: dataset
title: "SPECTRA: A Traceability Ontology for the 3GPP RAN Standardization Process"
abstract: >-
  SPECTRA is a reusable OWL 2 ontology for modeling the document types,
  relationships, and lifecycle of the 3GPP Radio Access Network (RAN)
  standardization process. The v1.0.1 release contains the ontology TTL,
  SHACL shapes, PyLODE HTML documentation, the full SpectraCQ v1.0
  dataset of 137 competency questions with verbatim company names
  matching the public 3GPP TDOC_List.xlsx — each with an executable
  SPARQL translation and the Cypher operational twin plus per-CQ
  verdict — a public replay harness (validate_sparql_parity.py;
  137/137 row-count parity against the released snapshot), a DCAT/VoID
  dataset description, onboarding and governance documentation
  (TUTORIAL.md, CONTRIBUTING.md), 15 representative Cypher and 6
  representative SPARQL queries, an end-to-end synthetic example, a
  metadata-only real-world mini instantiation, a metadata-only
  cross-WG process KG covering RAN1--RAN5, per-WG body-text knowledge
  graphs (sentence-level rendered text retained with explicit 3GPP
  source attribution, following the academic redistribution practice
  established by TSpec-LLM and the GSMA telecom-kg-rel19 release), the
  sanitized parsing pipeline source, reproducibility tests
  (verify_release.py; deterministic per-claim verifier whose check
  count varies with deposit layout), and a validation manifest mapping
  every quantitative claim in the accompanying paper to its supporting
  JSON evidence file. Raw Neo4j instance dumps and VectorDB embeddings
  are not bundled because they exceed the Zenodo size cap and are
  regenerable from the released body-text KGs and pipeline source.
